# Working files that should not be served from emr-inc.net.

# NOTE, 2026-10-05: this file governs the VERCEL deployment, which serves the
# apex as well as the subdomains. An earlier note here said the apex was GitHub
# Pages publishing the whole `main` root. That is wrong, and it cost a day: the
# issue 01 figure was pushed to main on the strength of it and 404ed, because
# Vercel serves emr-inc.net and nothing had deployed. A Vercel 404 page, not a
# Pages one, is what proved it.
#
# Two things follow. An entry here DOES withhold a file from emr-inc.net. And a
# push to main does NOT publish: Vercel's git integration is not connected, and
# the only thing that deploys is .github/workflows/open_data_daily.yml, on its
# schedule or on a push touching one of the three paths it watches. Committing
# an asset is not publishing it.
#
# Keeping a file out of the branch is still the only way to withhold it from
# anyone who can read the repository, which is what the dispatch capture needed.

DESIGN-BRIEF.md
MIGRATION.md
build-standalone.py
*-standalone.html
experiments/
dns/
design-lab/
